  "final_text": "All four steps are done. When I read the rule back, it showed as enabled with status ok.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Flights\" has `timestamp` as its time field. Its fields include `Carrier`, `Cancelled`, `Origin`, `Dest` and `AvgTicketPrice`.\n2. **Dashboard:** \"S4-06087acb Flights\" has two panels. \"Flights over time\" is a line chart of the flight count by `timestamp`. \"Flights by carrier\" is a bar chart of the flight count for the top 10 `Carrier` values.\n3. **Alert rule:** \"S4-06087acb Cancelled flights\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` arrive within 5 minutes. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. **Carrier panel edit:** The panel was already titled \"Flights by carrier\" from creation, so the edit left the title as it was.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
